{"id": "EUVD-2026-102568", "enisaUuid": "5b6b9464-cfe7-3c13-87a9-30c669b39c4f", "description": "Nezha from 2.2.5 before 2.3.15 contains an information disclosure vulnerability that allows authenticated users to retrieve third-party credentials because listDDNS omits WebhookURL and WebhookRequestBody redaction. Admins or PATs with nezha:ddns:read scope can call GET /api/v1/ddns to read cleartext tokens embedded in every user's DDNS webhook profiles.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T01:17:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T17:07:24", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/nezhahq/nezha/security/advisories/GHSA-hpfr-cmgc-f455", "https://github.com/nezhahq/nezha/commit/36b742a7e9a81ed782363dd19efd77b7030fbd0f", "https://github.com/nezhahq/nezha/commit/39d398066d8c644fe452f74704e34ada6c7ab61e", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/nezha-2.2.5-before-2.3.15-information-disclosure-via-ddns-list-endpoint"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111387", "GHSA-7922-f42v-j7c8"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.26, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "19c9052a-c03d-3b43-ad96-c6c94610a49d", "product": {"name": "nezha", "vendor": {"name": "nezhahq"}}, "product_version": "2.2.5 <2.3.15"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ea5dcf65-456c-38f2-9ce7-ad08d5cfc8b9", "vendor": {"name": "nezhahq"}}], "isExploited": false}